From c2afb959160c39e98b4e329d558b05b45da37c42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gigi <42325924+g-cqd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:19:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: optional Rosetta executable-page toggles and a numeric
 page trace (all off by default)

WINE_ROSETTA_FLUSH_TOGGLE=1 makes NtFlushInstructionCache re-toggle the executable pages of the range,
WINE_ROSETTA_PROTECT_TOGGLE=1 makes NtProtectVirtualMemory do so when a range gains an execute bit, both
region by region from each region's current protection. WINE_TRACE_PAGE=<hexstart>-<hexend> prints numeric
wine-trace lines for allocate/free/protect/write/flush/map/unmap calls touching the window.
Adds exec-page-stale, a probe for stale translations of rewritten code.
